{"kind":"assert","text":"Two questions on the a7c8072a ruling (a5d65e58) for the cutover head, now at ee1b72b9.\n\nStatus: the directory-partition-factory failure was a cutover fault, and ee1b72b9 fixes it. The cutover's sequence frames raise the app-lane proof from 8 to 9 frames. partitionReceiverPolicy's application branch applied the 8-frame base bound, so it returned null. The branch now uses the 16-frame identity bound, as partitionPublicationOrigin already does. The existing test at :97 is the witness.\n\narchive-installed fails 8 of 9:\n- 2 fail at :1449 on the decisions question (3bf7e5aa).\n- 1, \"Grow\", installs the retained old-spelling packet (Site 69424c1b, Room 5e2d34fa). It becomes the kept refusal test of your item 4 and expects invalid-application-package.\n- 4 (production, activation warm, activation evicted, \"old R17 Room A shape\") install the committed signed demo examples/grow/demo/application.dap.json, release 71e10ca9. A fifth, the production public archive command, fails because of them.\n\nProduction code binds to that signed demo. apps/room/archive-policy.ts:22-23 growArchivePolicies accepts only DEMO_RELEASE from DEMO_PUBLISHER with entry GROW_ARCHIVE_DEFINITIONS[0] (d2bc830e). apps/room/archive.ts:31 requires config.release === DEMO_RELEASE. The production scenarios run growArchivePolicies through archive-native-authority.ts:180 and :271. A demo built from current source and signed by the test signer fails each of these checks.\n\nQuestion 1. May the head pass the trusted release, publisher and entry into growArchivePolicies and the archive.ts config check as parameters, in place of the constants? worker.grow.ts passes DEMO_RELEASE, DEMO_PUBLISHER and GROW_ARCHIVE_DEFINITIONS, so production behaviour stays the same until you sign the new release. The tests pass a demo built from current source and signed by fixedSigner(254). GROW_ARCHIVE_DEFINITIONS stays the recorded pins. If a Grow digest appears that is not one of F's pins, the worker stops and I tell you.\n\nQuestion 2. The \"old R17 Room A shape\" test checks a published 37-pass history that advances from seq 146 on the recorded R17 package. Under your item 1 that package cannot install into a new-format room. Should the test move to the source-built demo, which drops its \"old R17\" claim, or retire with a note row that gives its acceptance case?\n\nI recommend yes to question 1. It is a signature change with no behaviour change, and your signed release in item 6 will need the same parameter. For question 2, I recommend that the test retire with a note row, unless its acceptance case (a 37-pass history advancing from seq 146) can be built from current source. In that case it moves and the note names the change."}